    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d870">

                <pb facs="1000" n="988" sameAs="frus:frus1943v02/pg988"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860H.20/101</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Yugoslav Chargé</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Rybář</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Assistant Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Berle</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-04-16">April 16, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Assistant Secretary</hi>: During the
                    conversation I had with you at the State Department two weeks ago, you had
                    expressed <pb facs="1001" n="989" xml:id="pg989"/> the desire to have some facts
                    concerning the activities of General Draža Mihajlovich and his army, as well as
                    the position of the so-called Partisans.</p>
                <p>I am pleased, therefore, to send to you enclosed a condensed exposition based on
                    facts and documents which the Yugoslav Embassy has received and which it
                    considers as trustworthy.</p>
                <p>Believe me [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dr. Vladimir Rybář</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d870-a1.xml" xpointer="d870-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
